  "current_question": "Continue autonomous CVRP research from the complete R12-A-fixed source tested as R13's candidate. This ordinary local starting tree includes the independently engineered common constructor repair; that operator-assisted repair is not an autonomous H/C discovery. It is not a promoted or retained-confirmed champion. R13 SCREENING ONLY was a provider-free, counterbalanced whole-bundle comparison against B0-fixed, not original B0. All 24 pairs were valid with no runtime, feasibility or fleet failures; 12 AB and 12 BA orders, equal dimension-based limits 60/90/120/180/240 seconds and canary 10 seconds. Case W/L/T 4/1/1, case-median distance improvement 91.5, bootstrap CI [-36,296.75], SCREENING_EXPAND_EXHAUSTED_CASE_LEVEL_UNCERTAIN / continue_explore, terminal NOT_CONFIRMED. This is not promotion. In seed order 120011/120017/120041/120047, B0-fixed minus candidate distances were: B-n34-k5 [0,0,0,0]; tai100a [163,301,200,156]; X-n351-k40 [648,368,367,328]; A-n54-k7 [0,3,2,1]; X-n190-k8 [0,-274,-144,134]; X-n513-k21 [226,226,226,226]. Corresponding case medians: 0,181.5,367.5,1.5,-72,226. Do not pool this contrast with R12's comparison to R11 B or historical original-B0 comparisons. R13 phase observations: tai100a candidate ALNS iterations [70,66,77,71] versus B0-fixed [25,26,30,37]. X-n351-k40 has zero ALNS in both arms for all four seeds; candidate initial VNS takes 138.476-138.556 seconds. X-n513-k21 candidate has zero ALNS and initial VNS 136.846-137.011 seconds; B0-fixed has one ALNS iteration per seed after 93.960-96.333 seconds of initial VNS. On X-n513 both arms' post-initial objectives equal their final objectives. The large-case effects therefore cannot be attributed to lazy worst removal or later ALNS learning. X-n190-k8 candidate iterations [2,4,3,2] versus B0-fixed [4,5,3,2]; candidate embedded VNS consumes 57.786-64.337 seconds of the approximately 69.84-second algorithm-local search allowance. Both arms start post-initial search at distance 17876; candidate subsequent gains [0,0,31,134] versus B0-fixed [0,274,175,0]. Candidate source has 15 destroy-repair pairs with randomized without-replacement first trials before learned selection, and segment_length=100: these 2-4 iterations never complete first trials or reach an in-loop segment update. This is an execution/source fact, not proof that any pair causes harm, not a required schedule or an activity gate. The inherited early phase handoff remains guarded by alns_threshold=2000 while screening has at most 512 customers, so it is inactive here. Best-improvement SWAP* still ranks all eligible route pairs before examining up to 10 pairs and 24 customer links per pair; a post-ranking cap does not itself bound ranking cost. These facts support source-grounded research, not a prescribed fix. Distinct R12 screening context: final A passed six-case expanded screening against R11 B, W/L/T 3/0/3, median +2.25, CI [0,11.25], 24 valid pairs; seed deltas 110017/110023/110039/110051 were B-n34-k5 [0,0,0,0], tai100a [17,53,19,-6], X-n351-k40 [-109,-75,84,99], A-n54-k7 [0,0,2,0], X-n190-k8 [0,-44,0,3], X-n513-k21 [28,8,8,8]. Both large cases had zero ALNS in both arms. A combined best-improvement SWAP* with lazy marginal-saving worst removal; the latter cannot explain the large-case effects. R12 final B failed its initial screen (1/1/1, median 0, CI [-45.5,10.5]); C's expanded 3/1/2, median 1.25, CI [-3.25,50.5] remained uncertain. Its two-pair cap followed exhaustive opportunity ranking, not the cheap bound initially proposed. All ten R12 ordinary history rows are appended in order, including the primary-target Contract rejection, rather than selecting only favorable results. Older R11 negative/uncertain candidates and R10's original-B0 screening pass remain separate historical contexts, not confirmations of this starting source. The four R4/R5/R6/R8 observations remain unchanged and R13 is a fifth distinct observation; complete ordered R3-R3i/R7/R9/R11/R12 scientific history is available to H. Can autonomous H/C improve this complete algorithm's distance quality and stability at the same budgets while preserving feasibility and fleet protection? Select the mechanism and implementation autonomously: no target file, mechanism, phase schedule, patch, required history action, novelty requirement or telemetry activity gate is prescribed. Current comparisons are against the fresh local R12-A-fixed champion (or a later local champion), not original B0 and not B0-fixed. Respect complete paired evidence and exact-candidate later-stage reuse. Private later-stage cases, outcomes and engineering regression diagnostics are deliberately absent from this input. R14 SCREENING ONLY, a separate autonomous campaign against the same complete R12-A-fixed local champion, completed twelve stages over ten evaluated cumulative candidates with 108 valid pairs and no promotion. All twelve ordinary R14 screening records are appended in order, including negative and uncertain results. Its first pair-weight candidate expanded to 2/0/4, median 0, CI [0,27.25]; its nearest-neighbor shortlist candidate expanded to 2/1/3, median 0, CI [-0.25,12.25]. Later initial screens had medians 0,0,0,0,-3.5,-60.5,0,-10 across the successive evaluated candidates, not isolated incremental effects. All 28 X-n351-k40 paired observations had zero ALNS in both arms. Several later proposals discussed X-n190-k8, but their three-case initial screens did not include X-n190-k8 or X-n513-k21; those claims were not tested on the named population. The last B proposal added a frozen-root one-hop frontier while the inherited per-call time quantum remained in the scheduler: its negative result describes that cumulative bundle, not an isolated replacement. None of the R14 final branch trees is selected or merged into this fresh starting source; the complete initial tree is still R12-A-fixed. This is an explicit fresh-source selection, not restoration or rollback of a live branch. For 